      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `Entities.escape()` handles supplementary characters (Unicode codepoints > U+FFFF) correctly: escaping to a hex entity reference when the charset can't encode them (ASCII), and passing through unchanged when it can (UTF-8). I'll improve understandability with named constants for the magic numbers, clearer variable names, and brief clarifying comments.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file extracts the magic number `135361` into a named constant `SUPPLEMENTARY_CODEPOINT` (with its hex equivalent `0x210C1` noted), names the `OutputSettings` variables clearly (`asciiSettings`, `utf8Settings`), and adds brief comments explaining *why* ASCII escapes the character while UTF-8 passes it through unchanged — all without altering the methods called, arguments, or expected outcomes."
    }
